######## S. Machine setup

$ kagebunshin next
kagebunshin is not set up on this machine
waiting on the human; tell them:
  - Please run `kagebunshin setup` in a terminal; it creates the local store, asking for its new passphrase, and starts and unlocks the daemon.
nothing more you can do until the human has done the above

(human) $ kagebunshin setup --no-service
New passphrase for the local store: 
Confirm: 
created $T/home/.config/kagebunshin
created the local store
the daemon is unlocked

next: name the folders of the projects to start with
  kagebunshin onboard DIR…
then, in each, paste this line into your coding agent:
  Set up kagebunshin here: run `kagebunshin next` and do what it says until it says done.

$ kagebunshin --help | grep -E '^  (onboard|next) '
  next       Print the next step toward a working setup of this checkout
  onboard    Start using kagebunshin in these checkouts, with one passphrase
